        position: "**A long-established Indian maker of cancer APIs, and one of very few integrated antibody-drug-conjugate makers in India**, per the company. Its API plants run near full; biologics and formulation plants are under-used (the company does not disclose by how much).",
        money: "Screener shows about **₹615cr of net debt** (₹660cr of borrowings less ₹45cr of cash). The company puts net debt at 1.3 times a year's operating profit, down from 6.7 times three years ago, and its credit rating was raised to AA-. It spent ₹114cr on capex in Q1 from its own cash, mostly on APIs and the peptide block. Free cash flow has been negative for twelve years. The balance sheet carries about ₹450cr of capitalised development spending, about ₹200cr of it more than three years old, and FY26 profit included ₹18.2cr from an associate whose accounts were unaudited. Promoters hold **40.1%**, down from 50.0% in September 2023; the last step, from 44.2%, was two family members being reclassified as public shareholders, not a sale.",
        watch: ["Return on capital rising from 12.5% towards the 18% it reports excluding biologics.", "The FY28 US launches, and a clean US re-inspection at Jadcherla.", "Profit without one-offs: tax back to about 25% and no associate gains."],
