        position: "**A category leader in iodinated contrast-media intermediates**, supplying the world's top contrast-media makers, and India's first saccharin maker.",
        money: "Net cash of **₹357cr** (Screener, March 2026): ₹44cr of borrowings against ₹149cr of cash and ₹252cr of investments. It raised ₹800cr from institutions on 9 July 2026 (1.58 crore new shares, about 8% dilution). It faces a ₹193cr income-tax demand over depreciation on goodwill, of which ₹128.7cr is already provided and ₹64.6cr of interest is carried as contingent. Vizag Phase 1 will cost about ₹1,000cr over three years (₹250cr in FY27), and ₹210cr is already spent at Mahad with ₹40cr to go. Promoters hold **73.2%** after the placement, down from 86% in December 2023.",
        watch: ["Year-on-year revenue growth returning.", "Mahad commercial batches by end-Q2 or early Q3 FY27.", "Any clear answer on Divi's contrast-media contracts."],
        charts: pharmaApiCharts['Blue Jet Healthcare'],
